<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Ingolstadt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1472">1472</a>–<a href="/years/1800">1800</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a> was founded in 1472 by Duke Louis IX the Rich of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a> as the first university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> it became a centre of Catholic theology, where Johann Eck taught, and later a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> stronghold. It moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> in 1800 and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> in 1826, and continues as the Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-ingolstadt.jpg" alt="University of Ingolstadt" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Karl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alte_Anatomie_Ingolstadt.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
